{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>To enter the נקרת.</b> A hollowed-out place." "<b>And in the clefts.</b> Like the shape of branches protruding from the rock, and they will hide there." "<b>To be terrified.</b> A transitive verb [lit. an outgoing verb]. And it is possible that אל תערוץ (Joshua 1:9) is likewise, lacking the word 'your heart.' And עריץ (Isaiah 29:20) is called an outgoing adjective [noun], like האמים (Genesis 14:5)."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:51:49.036721637Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}